    "items/thm-universal-property-of-the-enveloping-superalgebra.md": {
      "id": "thm-universal-property-of-the-enveloping-superalgebra",
      "deps": [
        "def-universal-enveloping-superalgebra",
        "def-associative-superalgebra-over-complex-numbers",
        "thm-universal-property-of-the-tensor-algebra"
      ],
      "aliases": [],
      "iota_lines": [
        "Let $\\mathfrak g$ be a complex Lie superalgebra, $A$ a unital associative superalgebra, and $\\phi:\\mathfrak g\\to A$ a parity-preserving linear map that preserves brackets, where the bracket on $A$ is its supercommutator. There is a unique unital associative-superalgebra homomorphism $\\widehat\\phi:U(\\mathfrak g)\\to A$ with $\\widehat\\phi\\circ\\iota=\\phi$.",
        "3.1 Therefore $\\widetilde\\phi$ factors through a unique homomorphism $\\widehat\\phi:T(\\mathfrak g)/I\\to A$, which has $\\widehat\\phi\\iota=\\phi$. Any other such homomorphism would pull back to an extension of $\\phi$ to $T(\\mathfrak g)$; uniqueness in [F3] makes it equal to $\\widehat\\phi$. [F1, F3, step 1.1, step 2.1] \u220e"
      ],
      "links_to_scope": [
        "def-universal-enveloping-superalgebra",
        "thm-universal-property-of-the-enveloping-superalgebra"
      ],
      "status": "draft"
    },
