      ],
      "aliases": [],
      "iota_lines": [
        "with the quotient multiplication is the **universal enveloping superalgebra**. Write $\\iota:\\mathfrak g\\to U(\\mathfrak g)$ for the degree-one map. The defining relation is",
        "$$ \\iota(x)\\iota(y)-(-1)^{|x||y|}\\iota(y)\\iota(x)=\\iota([x,y]). $$",
        "In particular, if $x$ is odd then $2\\iota(x)^2=\\iota([x,x])$, hence $\\iota(x)^2=\\tfrac12\\iota([x,x])$ over $\\mathbb C$. This quotient definition does not itself assert an ordered-monomial basis; the PBW basis is a separate theorem."
      ],
      "links_to_scope": [
